

with m as (
  returning id, course_slug, title, sort
)
select m.id, l.title, l.content, l.mins, l.sort
from m join (values
 ('ai-fundamentals',1,'How models learn','Large models are trained on huge amounts of text and learn the patterns of how ideas follow one another. Nothing is looked up; everything is predicted. That single fact explains most of AI''s strengths and every one of its failures.',12,1),
 ('ai-fundamentals',1,'Why AI sounds confident when it is wrong','A model has no sense of certainty. Fluency and accuracy are separate things. Treat every factual claim as a draft that needs a source.',10,2),
 ('ai-fundamentals',2,'Tasks worth delegating','Drafting, summarising, restructuring, translating, brainstorming and explaining. These are the jobs where AI reliably saves real time today.',12,1),
 ('ai-fundamentals',2,'Tasks to keep','Final judgement, relationships, taste, accountability and anything where being wrong is expensive.',10,2),
 ('ai-fundamentals',3,'Building a review habit','Every output gets a pass: is it true, is it yours, is it useful? Three questions, thirty seconds, most of the risk gone.',12,1),
 ('prompting-essentials',1,'The five parts','Give the model a role, the context, the task, the output format, and the constraints. Missing any one of these is the usual reason output feels generic.',12,1),
 ('prompting-essentials',1,'Show, don''t just tell','One good example of what you want beats three paragraphs describing it.',10,2),
 ('prompting-essentials',2,'The follow-up','Your second prompt is where quality happens. Ask it to critique its own answer, then improve it.',12,1),
 ('ai-safety-and-ethics',1,'Checking claims','Anything with a number, a name or a date gets verified before it leaves your hands.',10,1),
 ('ai-safety-and-ethics',2,'What never goes in a prompt','Client data, ID numbers, passwords, unreleased work and anything you would not put in an email to a stranger.',10,1),
 ('content-creation-with-ai',1,'Pick a lane','You cannot be interesting to everyone. Choose the intersection of what you know, what you enjoy and what people ask you about.',12,1),
 ('content-creation-with-ai',2,'One idea, five formats','Write once, then repurpose into video, carousel, thread, newsletter and short. AI makes the translation cheap.',15,1),
 ('content-creation-with-ai',3,'Publishing consistently','A modest post published weekly beats a brilliant one published never.',12,1),
 ('short-form-video',1,'Writing the hook','Name the tension in the first line. Curiosity, contradiction or a clear promise.',12,1),
 ('short-form-video',2,'A setup you will actually use','Phone, window light, a cheap mic and one editing tool you know well.',15,1),
 ('build-your-first-ai-project',1,'Choosing well','A good first project solves a problem you personally have, takes under two weeks, and can be shown in one screen.',12,1),
 ('build-your-first-ai-project',2,'Getting unstuck','When you stall, shrink the scope. A finished small thing teaches more than an abandoned big one.',15,1),
 ('build-your-first-ai-project',3,'Documenting it','Problem, approach, tools, result, what you would do differently. That is a portfolio entry.',12,1),
 ('career-readiness',1,'Skills audit','List what you can do, what you can prove, and the gap between them. The gap is your learning plan.',12,1),
 ('career-readiness',2,'Proof beats claims','Two documented projects will do more for you than any list of adjectives.',12,1),
 ('career-readiness',3,'Interview preparation','Prepare six stories: a success, a failure, a conflict, a decision, a learning moment and a thing you built.',15,1),
 ('data-literacy',1,'What averages hide','Distribution, outliers and sample size. Most bad decisions start with a mean.',12,1),
 ('data-literacy',2,'Making a recommendation','Data does not decide. You do. Say what you would do and why.',12,1),
 ('ai-for-business',1,'Finding the offer','Sell a specific outcome to a specific person. Vague offers are invisible.',15,1),
 ('ai-for-business',2,'Running lean','Templates, automations and AI drafting cover most of the admin a small business generates.',15,1),
 ('automate-your-workflow',1,'The time audit','Log a week. Anything you did more than three times identically is a candidate.',12,1),
 ('automate-your-workflow',2,'Automate one thing','Start with the smallest annoying task. Momentum matters more than ambition.',12,1)
) as l(course_slug,mod_sort,title,content,mins,sort)
on l.course_slug = m.course_slug and l.mod_sort = m.sort;





